<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<sdf version="1.6">
  <!-- Older PX4 sitl_run.sh spawns before Gazebo namespace discovery is ready.
       Match gz model's fallback namespace; the filename still selects the map.

       Geometry key (all values in metres, field 4.00 x 4.00):
         mat x = 0 .. 4   ->  gazebo x = -0.65 .. 3.35
         mat y = 0 .. 4   ->  gazebo y = -3.35 .. 0.65   (mat y is measured from
         the bottom edge of the printed mat, i.e. gazebo y = mat_y/1000 - 3.35)
       Takeoff pad is at mat (0.65, 3.35) -> gazebo (0.00, 0.00).

       The mat drawing annotates everything in MILLIMETRES.  Every element in
       this file has been reconciled against it - see
       tools/check_field_vs_drawing.py, which re-reads this file and prints
       "drawing value vs world value vs difference" for each one; it should
       report 0 FAIL.  tools/render_field.py draws the whole thing top-down
       with the drawing's dimension chain over it, which is the fastest way to
       see a mistake.

       The only element that did NOT match the drawing was the 危险品任务区
       column: the "1950" callout is measured from the right mat edge, so the
       column is mat x 2050 = gazebo x 1.40, while this file used to put it at
       1.50.  Cards and hazard_route were corrected together - they are a pair,
       change both or the aircraft hovers beside the card. -->
  <world name="default">
    <gravity>0 0 -9.81</gravity>
    <magnetic_field>6.0e-6 2.3e-5 -4.2e-5</magnetic_field>
    <!-- Match PX4 1c8ab2a0d7's lockstep assumptions from empty.world. -->
    <physics name="default_physics" default="0" type="ode">
      <ode>
        <solver>
          <type>quick</type>
          <iters>10</iters>
          <sor>1.3</sor>
          <use_dynamic_moi_rescaling>0</use_dynamic_moi_rescaling>
        </solver>
        <constraints>
          <cfm>0</cfm>
          <erp>0.2</erp>
          <contact_max_correcting_vel>100</contact_max_correcting_vel>
          <contact_surface_layer>0.001</contact_surface_layer>
        </constraints>
      </ode>
      <max_step_size>0.004</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1</real_time_factor>
      <real_time_update_rate>250</real_time_update_rate>
    </physics>
    <gui fullscreen="0">
      <camera name="field_camera">
        <pose>-3.5 -7.0 7.0 0 0.7 0.85</pose>
        <view_controller>orbit</view_controller>
      </camera>
    </gui>

    <scene>
      <ambient>0.55 0.55 0.55 1</ambient>
      <background>0.72 0.76 0.82 1</background>
      <shadows>true</shadows>
    </scene>

    <include>
      <uri>model://sun</uri>
    </include>

    <model name="competition_floor">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="floor_link">
        <collision name="floor_collision">
          <geometry>
            <box><size>4.0 4.0 0.04</size></box>
          </geometry>
          <pose>1.35 -1.35 -0.02 0 0 0</pose>
        </collision>
        <visual name="floor_visual">
          <geometry>
            <box><size>4.0 4.0 0.04</size></box>
          </geometry>
          <pose>1.35 -1.35 -0.02 0 0 0</pose>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.72 0.72 0.72 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.72 0.72 0.72 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- ===================================================================
         ALTITUDE BAND - read this before touching any z below.
         ===================================================================
         Every wall and every obstacle in this file now spans z 0.00 -> 3.00 m
         (pose z = 1.50, height/length = 3.00). Their xy footprints are
         untouched, so every route, waypoint and costmap in navigation_2d is
         still valid. Only the vertical extent moved.

         Why. Where the lidar actually flies, in metres:

             PX4 local z commanded by navigation_2d .... 1.500
           + iris model-origin offset in Gazebo ........ 0.116  (measured at
             arm time by px4_sensor_rig_node; see "odom origin aligned to PX4
             local frame: offset=(-0.007, 0.011, 0.116)")
           = iris model origin z ....................... 1.616
           + rig lidar mount (px4_sensor_rig/model.sdf,
             <pose>0 0 0.25</pose> above base_link) ..... 0.250
           = lidar plane, intended ..................... 1.866

         The same chain, but with the altitude bias this stack actually shows
         in the log ("Rig check: iris=(-0.39, -0.22, 1.90)" held at 1.89-1.91
         for the whole flight instead of 1.616), gives lidar plane = 2.150 m.

         The previous revision stopped every wall and obstacle at 2.00 m, i.e.
         0.15 m BELOW the 2.150 m plane - and only 0.134 m above the 1.866 m
         one. Gazebo's ray sensor does not drop an unmatched beam and does not
         return inf: it returns range_max (3.50). So Cartographer was handed a
         scan of 360 max-range phantoms with no wall, no obstacle and no loop
         closure. The front end then had nothing to constrain translation, the
         map grew to 5.55 x 7.85 m for a 4.05 x 4.05 m field ("Resizing
         costmap to 111 X 157 at 0.050000 m/pix"), map->odom drifted without
         bound until the odom route targets landed outside the costmap, DWA
         reported "failed to produce path", and the safety field finally
         tripped on the drifted map value.

         This band is 3.00 m tall, and it is 3.00 m for a reason that has
         nothing to do with the lidar: THE REAL VENUE'S FENCE IS 3 m TALL.
         Confirmed by the operator on 2026-09-25. So 3.00 m here is the
         faithful value and must NOT be "corrected" back to 2.00 m - the 2.00 m
         in the previous revision was simply wrong about the venue, and it
         happened to also sit below the lidar plane. Those are two independent
         facts, and treating them as one is what made this look like an
         altitude bug with an altitude fix. It never was: the fence was too
         short AND the revision had the wrong venue dimension, and fixing the
         dimension is what let the lidar see it.
         The lidar-plane numbers above are therefore kept only as evidence for
         why the old value was fatal; they are not the reason for the value.

         STILL OPEN: the six obstacles (fixed_obstacle_1..4, random_obstacle_1
         and _2) were raised to 3.00 m in the same edit, but the drawing
         annotates those bars at 2.00 m high. If the real bars are 2.00 m and
         the real lidar flies at ~1.75 m they are still seen, so this changes
         no behaviour in either 2D navigation or scan matching - which is why
         they were left at 3.00 m rather than churned. Confirm the venue's bar
         height before treating 3.00 as authoritative for them; the walls are
         confirmed, the bars are not.

         Walls: thickness 0.05 m, sitting just outside the mat edge, so the
         clear inner area is exactly x [-0.65, 3.35], y [-3.35, 0.65] - i.e.
         the printed 4x4 mat and the 0.20 m safety margin used by
         navigation_2d are unchanged.
         =================================================================== -->
    <model name="perimeter_wall_north">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>1.35 0.675 1.50 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="wall_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><box><size>4.00 0.05 3.00</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>4.00 0.05 3.00</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.34 0.37 0.41 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.44 0.47 0.52 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="perimeter_wall_south">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>1.35 -3.375 1.50 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="wall_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><box><size>4.00 0.05 3.00</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>4.00 0.05 3.00</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.34 0.37 0.41 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.44 0.47 0.52 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="perimeter_wall_west">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>-0.675 -1.35 1.50 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="wall_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><box><size>0.05 4.10 3.00</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>0.05 4.10 3.00</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.34 0.37 0.41 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.44 0.47 0.52 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="perimeter_wall_east">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>3.375 -1.35 1.50 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="wall_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><box><size>0.05 4.10 3.00</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>0.05 4.10 3.00</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.34 0.37 0.41 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.44 0.47 0.52 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- Fixed obstacle 1 (固定障碍物1): 0.10 m wide, 1.70 m long, 3.00 m tall
         (see ALTITUDE BAND above - the drawing says 2.00 m, the lidar flies at
         1.87-2.15 m, so 2.00 m is invisible to it).
         Drawing: bar left face 1300 mm from the left mat edge, top flush with
         the field edge -> mat x 1300..1400, mat y 2300..4000.
         Gazebo centre = (0.70, -0.20). -->
    <model name="fixed_obstacle_1">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0.70 -0.20 1.50 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="obstacle_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><box><size>0.10 1.70 3.00</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>0.10 1.70 3.00</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.20 0.20 0.22 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.24 0.24 0.28 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- Fixed obstacle 2 (固定障碍物2): 1.60 m long, 45 deg, 3.00 m tall
         (see ALTITUDE BAND above).
         Drawing: 45 deg bar nested in the top-right corner - its lower-left end
         corner sits at mat (2800, 2800) and its upper-right end corners touch
         the top and right mat edges.  The bounding square of such a bar is
         (1600 + 100)/sqrt(2) = 1202 mm, centred on mat (3400, 3400).
         Gazebo centre = (2.75, 0.048) -> rounded to (2.75, 0.05). -->
    <model name="fixed_obstacle_2">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>2.75 0.05 1.50 0 0 0.785398</pose>
      <link name="obstacle_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><box><size>1.60 0.10 3.00</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>1.60 0.10 3.00</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.20 0.20 0.22 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.24 0.24 0.28 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- Fixed obstacles 3 and 4 (固定障碍物3 / 固定障碍物4): 0.10 m wide, 0.50 m
         deep, 3.00 m tall (see ALTITUDE BAND above; the old comment here said
         "0.50 m high" but 0.50 is the y extent - they were 2.00 m high, and
         2.00 m is below the lidar plane).
         Both are flush with the bottom mat edge: mat y 3500..4000 -> gazebo
         y -3.10.
         Drawing bottom chain "1300 | 1400 | 100 | 1200" = 4000:
           obstacle 3 left face  1300 mm -> centre mat x 1350 -> gazebo 0.70
           obstacle 4 left face  2700 mm -> centre mat x 2750 -> gazebo 2.10 -->
    <model name="fixed_obstacle_3">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0.70 -3.10 1.50 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="obstacle_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><box><size>0.10 0.50 3.00</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>0.10 0.50 3.00</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.20 0.20 0.22 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.24 0.24 0.28 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="fixed_obstacle_4">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>2.10 -3.10 1.50 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="obstacle_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><box><size>0.10 0.50 3.00</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>0.10 0.50 3.00</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.20 0.20 0.22 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.24 0.24 0.28 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- Random obstacles (随机障碍物1 / 随机障碍物2): 0.10 m radius, 3.00 m tall
         (see ALTITUDE BAND above - 2.00 m is below the lidar plane).
         The mat marks two candidate
         positions per column, 1000 mm / 500 mm apart on a 500 mm grid measured
         from the bottom mat edge:
             left  column, mat x 1350 -> gazebo x 0.70
                     "1" mat y 1900 -> gazebo y -1.45   (used below)
                     "2" mat y  900 -> gazebo y -2.45
             right column, mat x 2750 -> gazebo x 2.10
                     "1" mat y 1900 -> gazebo y -1.45   (used below)
                     "2" mat y 1400 -> gazebo y -1.95
         This world ships the both-"1" draw; swap in the "2" poses if the live
         draw differs. -->
    <model name="random_obstacle_1">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0.70 -1.45 1.50 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="obstacle_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.10</radius><length>3.00</length></cylinder></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.10</radius><length>3.00</length></cylinder></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.85 0.30 0.10 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.90 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="random_obstacle_2">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>2.10 -1.45 1.50 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="obstacle_link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.10</radius><length>3.00</length></cylinder></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.10</radius><length>3.00</length></cylinder></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.85 0.30 0.10 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.90 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- Start pad (起飞点): mat (650, 3350) = the takeoff cross on the drawing,
         which is the PX4 home position -> gazebo (0, 0). -->
    <model name="takeoff_pad">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 0 0.006 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="pad_link">
        <visual name="pad">
          <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.20</radius><length>0.012</length></cylinder></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.10 0.55 0.20 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.10 0.65 0.25 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- ===================================================================
         TASK-ZONE MARKERS - 危险品任务区 / 人员救助任务区
         ===================================================================
         Both task zones carry a printed marker on the mat: a framed square
         card.  The drawing draws each of them twice over - a thick coloured
         border with an obvious edge, and the sign face inside it:

             危险品任务区   厚红框 + 白底 + 黄底黑边三角形警告标志 (GB 2894)
             人员救助任务区 厚浅蓝框 + 白底 + 人像卡

         So each marker here is built the same way, in two pieces:

           frame_*   real geometry, not a texture.  Outer 0.45 x 0.45 m,
                     0.025 m wide bars, 0.010 m tall, so the border stands
                     2 mm proud of the card and reads as an edge marking from
                     any camera angle - a flat printed border disappears at a
                     raking angle, which is why the frames were not visible
                     before.
           face      a 0.40 x 0.40 x 0.008 m box textured from
                     model://gc_task_markers.  That model is a resource
                     container (textures + OGRE material script); the markers
                     stay inline here so tools/check_config.py can still read
                     their footprints straight out of this file.

         NO <collision> anywhere in these markers.  They are 10 mm tall, the
         aircraft flies at 1.20-1.50 m, and the costmap must not see a 0.45 m
         obstacle sitting on a task waypoint.  check_config.py's
         _world_footprints() drops them on height for the same reason.

         COLOUR CONTRACT with navigation_2d/src/mission_vision.cpp - do not
         "tidy" the textures without re-reading it:
           hazard  mask = HSV H[15,40] S>=70 V>=70   -> the safety yellow of
                   the triangle.  The black pictogram and the black triangle
                   border are holes inside that yellow, and RETR_EXTERNAL
                   ignores holes, so the blob stays one big triangle.
           person  mask = HSV H[75,125] S>=55 V>=70  -> the blue frame ring.
                   Its external contour is the full 0.45 m square, ~4x10^4 px
                   at the 1.2 m task height, far above person_min_area=500.
         =================================================================== -->

    <!-- 危险品任务区 #1: 易燃 (GB 2894 当心火灾 / 易燃).
         Drawing: "1950" callout from the right mat edge -> mat x 2050.
         Hazards are a column, unlike the obstacles. -->
    <model name="hazard_zone_card_1">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>1.40 0.00 0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="card_link">
        <visual name="sign_face">
          <pose>0 0 0.004 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.40 0.40 0.008</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <script>
              <uri>model://gc_task_markers/materials/scripts</uri>
              <uri>model://gc_task_markers/materials/textures</uri>
              <name>GC/Sign/Flammable</name>
            </script>
          </material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="frame_south">
          <pose>0 -0.2125 0.005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.45 0.025 0.010</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.70 0.02 0.02 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="frame_north">
          <pose>0 0.2125 0.005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.45 0.025 0.010</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.70 0.02 0.02 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="frame_west">
          <pose>-0.2125 0 0.005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.025 0.40 0.010</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.70 0.02 0.02 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="frame_east">
          <pose>0.2125 0 0.005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.025 0.40 0.010</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.70 0.02 0.02 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- 危险品任务区 #2: 易爆 (GB 2894 当心爆炸).
         Drawing: the two red frames sit 454 mm apart centre to centre and are
         nearly touching; the frame here is 0.45 m so the centres are 0.45 m
         apart -> gazebo y 0.00 / -0.45.
         Swap the material name to make this card whichever hazard the task
         sheet names.  All nine ship:
           GC/Sign/Flammable          1-02 当心火灾
           GC/Sign/Explosive          1-03 当心爆炸
           GC/Sign/Corrosive          1-04 当心腐蚀
           GC/Sign/Toxic              1-05 当心中毒
           GC/Sign/Biohazard          1-06 当心生物危害
           GC/Sign/IonizingRadiation  1-27 当心电离辐射
           GC/Sign/Fissionable        1-28 当心裂变物质
           GC/Sign/Oxidizer           1-42 当心氧化物
           GC/Sign/GasCylinder        1-43 当心高压气瓶
         (tools/make_task_markers.py regenerates all of them from the standard;
         tools/assets/gb2894/reference/ holds the originals to compare against.) -->
    <model name="hazard_zone_card_2">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>1.40 -0.45 0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="card_link">
        <visual name="sign_face">
          <pose>0 0 0.004 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.40 0.40 0.008</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <script>
              <uri>model://gc_task_markers/materials/scripts</uri>
              <uri>model://gc_task_markers/materials/textures</uri>
              <name>GC/Sign/Explosive</name>
            </script>
          </material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="frame_south">
          <pose>0 -0.2125 0.005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.45 0.025 0.010</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.70 0.02 0.02 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="frame_north">
          <pose>0 0.2125 0.005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.45 0.025 0.010</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.70 0.02 0.02 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="frame_west">
          <pose>-0.2125 0 0.005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.025 0.40 0.010</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.70 0.02 0.02 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="frame_east">
          <pose>0.2125 0 0.005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.025 0.40 0.010</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.70 0.02 0.02 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.05 0.05 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- 人员救助任务区: three portrait cards in a column, drawing "650"
         from the right mat edge -> mat x 3350 -> gazebo x 2.70, and the outer
         frame of card 3 sits on the "500" line -> mat y 500 -> card centre
         gazebo y -2.65, cards then pitched 0.80 m.
         navigation_2d.launch routes person_route to exactly those three y. -->
    <model name="person_zone_card_1">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>2.70 -1.05 0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="card_link">
        <visual name="sign_face">
          <pose>0 0 0.004 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.40 0.40 0.008</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <script>
              <uri>model://gc_task_markers/materials/scripts</uri>
              <uri>model://gc_task_markers/materials/textures</uri>
              <name>GC/Sign/Person</name>
            </script>
          </material>
        </visual>
        <visual name="frame_south">
          <pose>0 -0.2125 0.005 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.45 0.025 0.010</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.22 0.58 0.88 1</ambient><diffuse>0.30 0.70 0.95 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
